L2 Knowledge Base - Issue 1 (Login)
v 1.0, 07/08/2026, status : Draft

Purpose
Restore floor-wide slow/failed sign-in service after Win11 and Intune change activity.

Trigger
Use when multiple users on Floor 6 report slow or failed sign-in.

Required access
- Intune admin permissions
- Entra sign-in log access
- Local admin on at least one affected endpoint
- Incident and change record access

Procedure (navigation > action > expected)
1. Service desk > Incident > Open ticket > Set In Progress.
Expected: ownership and timestamp captured.
2. Service desk > Work notes > Record affected user and host.
Expected: fixed test pair established.
3. Endpoint > PowerShell (admin) > Run dsregcmd /status.
Expected: join and token state captured.
4. Endpoint > Event Viewer > Security > Export last 2h IDs 4624/4625/4771/4776.
Expected: authentication evidence exported.
5. Endpoint > Event Viewer > User Profiles Service/Operational > Export last 2h.
Expected: profile evidence exported.
6. Intune > Devices > Affected device > Sync.
Expected: fresh policy check requested.
7. Intune > Configuration profiles > Suspected sign-in/profile policy > Assignments.
Expected: pre-change assignment snapshot captured.
8. Intune > Same policy > Pause/unassign for Floor 6 scope only.
Expected: suspected policy stops applying to Floor 6.
9. Intune > Affected device > Sync again.
Expected: updated effective policy requested.
10. Endpoint > Sign-in with affected user.
Expected: desktop reached within normal timing.
11. Repeat with second user/device.
Expected: confirms floor-level recovery.

Verification
- Affected user sign-in succeeds.
- Second user sign-in succeeds.
- No repeating auth/profile pattern during monitoring window.
- Intune sync status shows success on tested devices.

Rollback
1. Restore exact pre-change policy assignment scope.
2. Sync tested devices.
3. Reboot tested devices once.
4. Re-test sign-in.
5. Escalate with logs and assignment diff if still degraded.
